{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>A heifer of three years.</b> Three heifers — a hint to the three bulls: the bull of Yom Kippur, the bull of the court's inadvertent ruling, and the heifer whose neck is broken." "<b>And a she-goat of three years.</b> A hint to the goat offered inside, the additional goats of the Festival, and the sin-offering of an individual." "<b>And a ram of three years.</b> A certain guilt-offering, a suspended guilt-offering, and a ewe-lamb for the sin-offering of an individual." "<b>And a turtledove and a young bird.</b> A turtledove and a young dove (Bereshit Rabbah)."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:58:49.400044148Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}